#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124112 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e593685-f5ca-5501-94bf-7cb4d49e935b" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Function Involving Reciprocals and Radicals"}] :question/id #uuid "a2c947c7-9873-5137-91ca-4fe0b42e9bb7" :question/math-academy-id "e-11021" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z = \\dfrac {\\sqrt {y+1}}{x+y}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/6fa2a35bd31547c7ee3931d9c21defc69be918fb57c8ceb26ce9f19e1a77c816.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, y \\geq -1, \\: y \\neq -x \\big\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124113 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e4fd256-a726-523c-84dc-f62d4e2711cc" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Domain of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/id #uuid "42cbeba7-685e-5782-9695-9671d16b7f80" :question/math-academy-id "e-11022" :question/problem "Sketch the domain of $g(x,y)=\\dfrac{1}{\\ln(x+y)}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/b3e80f16cf1d83b9e6936a77fbd8c165a610bc5bff73b39521b03058e5b066b2.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD = \\left \\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\, : \\, y \\gt -x, \\, y \\neq 1-x \\right \\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we plot the corresponding domain. \n\n- Starting with $y> -x,$ we draw a dashed line $y=-x$ and shade the region *above* the line.\n\n- Then, we draw a dashed line $y=1-x$ through the shaded region.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/6aa1aaeadb177cf5a80bcb12a247725cb3396586e7516c3ba30b46b03a9d2612.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124114 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9289c4d-4f7f-5704-a2cb-272f92d8fef3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Two-Variable Function"}] :question/id #uuid "59fa0287-0562-5cf2-8469-946a69dc8adf" :question/math-academy-id "e-11025" :question/problem "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as \n\n$$\nf(x,y) = y^2 - \\log_3(x - 7).\n$$\n\nEvaluate this function at the point $(10,3).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(10,3),$ we substitute $x = 10$ and $y = 3$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(10,3) & =({y}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(x-7)){|}_{(10,3)} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(10-7) \\\\  & =9-{log}_{3}⁡(3) \\\\  & =9-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(10,3)=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124116 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88f2bc84-03e8-5921-81e2-683a09195279" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Function Containing Exponential, Logarithmic, and Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "bdae9fe0-a491-531b-ac36-7a37d2c32f16" :question/math-academy-id "e-11029" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z= \\dfrac{\\ln (2x+y)}{\\sqrt{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive,\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y>0 \\\\ x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{(x, y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, 2x+y >0, \\: x > 0 \\big\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313941 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e593685-f5ca-5501-94bf-7cb4d49e935b" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Function Involving Reciprocals and Radicals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbf1b557-d5bb-5d33-8348-e4e43d82a976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313943} {:answer/id #uuid "b4203380-9bf8-53df-94da-1c518f20f749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313944} {:answer/id #uuid "2074cbff-74d9-5585-b2e3-5546c96a7d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313945} {:answer/id #uuid "51aaf4e3-28c1-5d53-b891-0861b33e391d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313946} {:answer/id #uuid "1b3337a9-e1b0-5c41-adef-a1e7cc733f92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51aaf4e3-28c1-5d53-b891-0861b33e391d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313946} :answer-field/id #uuid "29a1827a-34d3-5733-9df6-476434b30016" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313942}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ffc177d-b73e-54a6-8456-b4975b1494ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-158179" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88f2bc84-03e8-5921-81e2-683a09195279" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Function Containing Exponential, Logarithmic, and Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ab18917-d118-537c-ba2c-0019eef305da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x + y > 0, y > 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121310} {:answer/id #uuid "061c8f9b-5d90-51c7-93fe-5fcbf78738e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x + y > 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121311} {:answer/id #uuid "45e31821-954b-5468-8ae1-98d19db3c4b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121312} {:answer/id #uuid "761e8907-452b-5e2f-b048-5c5a6d10ed52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x + y \\ge 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121313} {:answer/id #uuid "76cd8e3e-7787-5f79-8fc3-c4d6a6a804d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x + y > 0, y \\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76cd8e3e-7787-5f79-8fc3-c4d6a6a804d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x + y > 0, y \\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121314} :answer-field/id #uuid "94f50ade-4552-58dd-a8a7-e1fd7b897ae1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a0dae25-b4dd-5e0a-a533-db76e6eac14c" :question/math-academy-id "q-158180" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)}{y}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y>0 \\\\ y\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y>0,\\,y\\ne 0}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88f2bc84-03e8-5921-81e2-683a09195279" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Function Containing Exponential, Logarithmic, and Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4a72dc0-014e-5258-a6e2-cedbaa689497" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: - \\frac{π}{2} \\le x - y \\le \\frac{π}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121316} {:answer/id #uuid "eb95cc26-4d4d-5434-8402-984131fba02c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: - 1 \\le x - y \\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121317} {:answer/id #uuid "0765aea4-bb63-528e-b898-0e9b16cb285b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: 0 \\le x - y \\le π}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121318} {:answer/id #uuid "362c1830-50ac-551b-a829-b0664c20bd5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: - 1 \\le x - y \\le 1, x > 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121319} {:answer/id #uuid "50565c29-0949-5f77-a533-5e5be08ee5f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb95cc26-4d4d-5434-8402-984131fba02c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: - 1 \\le x - y \\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121317} :answer-field/id #uuid "12b84214-0f00-5017-89b8-b080f2844876" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8d83dba6-238e-5ccd-970d-da3225e73ce3" :question/math-academy-id "q-158181" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function  $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x-y).$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The argument of the arccosine has values between $-1$ and $1.$\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n-1\\le x-y\\le 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le x-y\\le 1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124717 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e593685-f5ca-5501-94bf-7cb4d49e935b" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Function Involving Reciprocals and Radicals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d5139b5-777d-5b5f-aa2c-ee30f38fc91d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x^{2} + y^{2} < 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121322} {:answer/id #uuid "9fde8b31-429f-5efd-8535-5cf75fd39adc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121323} {:answer/id #uuid "adc8c887-4013-56cc-97dc-77d7d8a46fcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x^{2} + y^{2} = 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121324} {:answer/id #uuid "f8075557-d867-5c8f-82de-f27b8127b64b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x^{2} + y^{2} \\ge 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121325} {:answer/id #uuid "01eebee0-8f70-583a-8613-6a33fc0b6f38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x^{2} + y^{2} \\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01eebee0-8f70-583a-8613-6a33fc0b6f38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: x^{2} + y^{2} \\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121326} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a3ae45b-e880-5c35-952d-da13917b47e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b8f769a-fcb4-5284-aeb5-6002c7cc37e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-158182" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e4fd256-a726-523c-84dc-f62d4e2711cc" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Domain of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a66a8f10-8e09-56e7-8241-aae382a5d61a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Devel